          <avActivityHighlights>Individual avalanche prone locations are to be found on wind-loaded slopes at intermediate and high altitudes.</avActivityHighlights>
          <avActivityComment>The avalanche prone locations are very rare. They are to be found on extremely steep shady slopes in high Alpine regions and on wind-loaded slopes. As a consequence of solar radiation individual small natural moist avalanches are possible. Restraint should be exercised because avalanches can sweep people along and give rise to falls. The Avalanche Warning Service currently has only a small amount of information that has been collected in the field.</avActivityComment>
          <snowpackStructureComment>15 to 30 cm of snow fell in the last few days above approximately 1600 m. The moderate wind has transported some snow. The new snow is loosely bonded on wind-protected shady slopes. As a consequence of solar radiation a crust will form on the surface.</snowpackStructureComment>
